        "original_id": "a7407eea-3168-5c01-9395-4e5b5de1c97b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Alvin Toffler, Isaac Bashevis Singer\n- Works: Future Shock, A Day Of Pleasure: Stories of a Boy Growing Up in Warsaw, A Crown of Feathers and Other Stories\n- Awards: U.S. National Book Awards\n- Topics: Futurism, modern technologies, digital revolution, communication revolution\n\nFacts:\n- Alvin Toffler was born on October 4, 1928.\n- Future Shock is a 1970 book written by futurist Alvin Toffler.\n- Isaac Bashevis Singer won a 1970 U.S. National Book Award in Children's Literature for his memoir A Day Of Pleasure: Stories of a Boy Growing Up in Warsaw.\n- Isaac Bashevis Singer won a 1974 U.S. National Book Award in Fiction for his collection A Crown of Feathers and Other Stories.\n- Alvin Toffler was an American writer, futurist, and businessman known for discussing modern technologies, including the digital revolution and the communication revolution, with emphasis on their effects on cultures worldwide.\n- Alvin Toffler died on June 27, 2016.",
